<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Heinrich Parler</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1300–c. 1370</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Heinrich Parler the Elder</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Heinrich Parler was a German master builder from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cologne">Cologne</a> who worked in Schwäbisch Gmünd, where from 1351 he built the choir of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-cross-minster">Holy Cross Minster</a>, one of the first late Gothic hall churches in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. He founded the Parler family of architects and sculptors; his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-parler">Peter Parler</a> built <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/st-vitus-cathedral">St. Vitus Cathedral</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague">Prague</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/heinrich-parler.jpg" alt="Heinrich Parler" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Beckstet at German Wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gmuend_Muenster_von_Suedwest.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote><b>Heinrich Parler</b> began the Holy Cross Minster there in the 14th century, one of the first German hall churches in the late Gothic style, and his son Peter Parler went on to build Prague Cathedral.</blockquote><a href="/state/free-imperial-city-of-schwabisch-gmund">Free Imperial City of Schwäbisch Gmünd</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cologne">Cologne</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a>. Died in Schwäbisch Gmünd, in what is now <a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=50.94,6.96&amp;year=1345" aria-label="Cologne on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4708 397 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Heinrich Parler"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5158 667h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5158 667h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=50.94,6.96&amp;year=1345">What was here in 1345? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
